Experimental YOLO11n detector for LibreYOLO

The convolution blocks, anchor and distribution decoding, task-aligned
assignment, detection loss and portions of the training transforms are
reused from LibreYOLO's YOLO9 implementation. Its upstream is
https://github.com/MultimediaTechLab/YOLO/tree/c4cb5f6f56102eceeaa7d75e23e1125cd0373eaf
under the MIT license reproduced below.

The shared training pipeline uses mosaic placement and exponential moving
average code derived from YOLOX (https://github.com/Megvii-BaseDetection/YOLOX),
Copyright (c) 2021-2022 Megvii Inc. All rights reserved. The shared
postprocessor uses pre-NMS candidate filtering adapted from MMDetection
(https://github.com/open-mmlab/mmdetection/tree/cfd5d3a985b0249de009b67d04f37263e11cdf3d),
Copyright (c) OpenMMLab. All rights reserved. Both components are licensed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0. See the distributed Apache-2.0.txt
and the YOLOX and mmdetection entries in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt.

PORT.md credits the CC BY 4.0 papers used for architectural descriptions,
identifies the decoder contract references, and records the experimental
preset choices. The tower implementation provenance is tracked there.

